WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.760
Tesla's Optimus Factory Construction is accelerating at gigatexas ahead of 2027 sales. This is Tesla Shorts Time,

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:14.400
episode 610. Construction of the dedicated Optimus Factory at gigatexas is accelerating.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:21.660
The timeline targets volume production in 2027. Tesla confirmed plans to begin selling Optimus

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:28.660
robots in 2027. The announcement aligns with ongoing factory construction at gigatexas. Production

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.380
Action capacity is being prepared at the Texas site.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:37.380
The Tesla app added Optimus Charger support with five specific details now available to

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:37.680
users.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.080
The update enables new charging features for the robot.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:45.080
Users can access the new Optimus charging options directly.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.520
The support update rolled out with the latest app version.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:54.880
Tesla's FSD supervised software completed its first full year in Australia and New Zealand.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.120
and collisions dropped 40% during that period.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.620
The 40% reduction covers the full 12 months.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:04.980
Supervised FSD recorded the safety improvement

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:05.960
across the region.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.520
Tesla reported 1 million unsupervised miles

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.880
accumulated by the CyberCab in Austin.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.780
The milestone was achieved on public roads.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.980
The CyberCab reached the total

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.700
in unsupervised operation.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.900
Austin is the location where the miles were logged.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:26.600
Top Gear Tech toured the Nevada facility and wrote a finished Tesla semi.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.880
The tour showed active production of the electric truck.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.000
The finished vehicle was driven as part of the visit.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.040
The production Tesla semi shows improved speed and efficiency.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:41.020
The latest version delivers higher performance than earlier prototypes.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.380
Efficiency gains were confirmed in the production model.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:49.020
Tesla reopened roadster reservations in Canada and the United States.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:55.900
The move precedes the October 1st Global Reveal. Reservations are now available again in both countries.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.360
Global availability follows the North American window.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:05.880
A new Jersey home buyer reported that the discontinued Tesla solar roof led to an insurance review at closing.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.980
The policy review occurred because the product is no longer offered.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.640
Insurance carriers questioned coverage for the repired system.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:18.780
A Tesla Solar customer stated that 100-degree heat halted the installation.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.620
The new Powerwall remained at 2% charge during the delay.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:26.320
Extreme temperatures prevented crews from completing the work.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:29.440
The battery stayed at minimal charge throughout the pause.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.960
Installation resumed only after temperatures dropped.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:37.540
Tesla's Optimus program now faces competition from Figure AI.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:42.140
Figure AI is positioned as a new challenger in the humanoid space.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.800
The Optimus Timeline remains the reference point in the report.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.840
Competition enters the picture alongside the 2027 target.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:55.240
Tesla has not commented on how it will handle warranty or replacement support for owners

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.500
of the retired product.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:02.940
Tesla Roddy issued a direct warning today after discovering that Tesla Roddy.org is actively

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:08.300
mirroring the outlet's content and publishing entirely fabricated stories under the same name

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.000
and branding.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.860
The fake domain copies the original site's layout and logo without permission.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:19.980
The outlet's post explicitly asks readers and the community for advice on next steps to address

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:25.440
the impersonation. The warning stresses that any articles appearing on the mirrored domain should

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:31.560
be treated as unreliable. Multiple instances of invented headlines and altered details have already

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:37.980
surfaced on the Copycat site. Tesla Roddy emphasized that only stories on its verified channels represent

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.020
an accurate reporting.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.060
An owner shared a post today expressing hope

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.420
that Tesla's production lines will soon scale

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:47.200
to match the current high level of demand for its vehicles.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:50.060
The comment pointed specifically to the gap

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.540
between incoming orders and available output.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.980
Production scaling remains the central concern raised

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:56.540
in the message.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.220
The post appeared on the platform this morning,

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:01.740
alongside other notes about factory readiness.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:05.580
No timeline for closing that gap was provided in the update.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:15.580
Another comment from the same account highlighted that a large new facility will be required to handle upcoming vehicle programs, noting the physical size needed for the builds.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:19.660
The remark focused on the scale of infrastructure still required.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:24.160
It referenced a specific person named Gary in connection with the planning.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:29.000
The post arrived alongside the demand capacity discussion earlier today.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:38.800
The economics of humanoid robot production hinge less on the final assembly line and more on the cost and availability of high-strength magnets and actuators.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:49.680
Tesla's public timeline for Optimus Sales in 2027 assumes those supply chains can scale without the multi-year lead times that have constrained other precision manufacturers.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:56.300
measures. Securing consistent volumes of Neodymium iron boron magnets at stable prices becomes

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:03.060
the gating factor rather than robot software or final integration steps. A single ND FEB

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:08.560
magnet set per robot already carries material costs that rival the entire bill of materials

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:14.700
for many consumer electronics. If Tesla must secure new sources or vertically integrate magnet

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:20.660
production. The per-unit price target moves from competitive with human labor to merely comparable.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:27.220
Early supplier qualification data will determine whether the 2027 pricing goal holds or requires

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:33.280
adjustment. Before we go, the next supplier updates on magnet volumes will show whether the

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:38.560
addressable market stays broad or narrows. That covers it for today's Tesla developments.

